#. type: Title =
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/schedule/forecasts.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "OpenEMS: Forecasts for consumption and production"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/schedule/forecasts.adoc
msgid ""
"Several functions need a look into the future: xref:user/storage-control/"
"grid-optimized-charge.adoc[Grid-optimized charge] wants to know when the "
"solar surplus ends. xref:user/storage-control/time-of-use-tariffs.adoc[Price "
"control] wants to know how much electricity is needed in the expensive "
"hours. For this purpose, OpenEMS creates **forecasts for solar yield and "
"consumption**, in quarter hours for today and tomorrow."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/schedule/forecasts.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "The available forecasting methods"
msgstr ""

#. type: Table
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/schedule/forecasts.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Method\n"
"| for\n"
"| Idea\n"
"\n"
"| “Same as yesterday” (Persistence)\n"
"| any values\n"
"| Yesterday's curve repeats itself.\n"
"| “Same weekday” (Similar Day)\n"
"| Consumption\n"
"| Average of the same weekdays over the last 4 weeks.\n"
"| Daily profiles (Profile Clustering)\n"
"| Consumption\n"
"| Learns the typical daily routines of the household.\n"
"| Weather model\n"
"| Solar yield\n"
"| Learns how much your own system delivers in which weather.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/schedule/forecasts.adoc
msgid ""
"Several methods can be set up. An order determines which one is asked first. "
"If it returns nothing, the next one is used. If a total value (e.g. total "
"production) has no forecast of its own, OpenEMS combines it from the "
"forecasts of the individual producers."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/schedule/forecasts.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "“Same as yesterday”"
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-same-as-yesterday
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/schedule/forecasts.adoc
msgid ""
"The simplest method. It needs no learning phase and works from the second "
"day. It cannot foresee weather changes, weekends or special days."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/schedule/forecasts.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "“Same weekday”"
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-same-weekday
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/schedule/forecasts.adoc
msgid ""
"For a Monday, the average of the last four Mondays is used. This captures "
"weekly rhythms, e.g. home office days or laundry days. After the clocks "
"change, the pattern is shifted by one hour for a few weeks."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/schedule/forecasts.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "Daily profiles (consumption)"
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-daily-profiles-consumption
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/schedule/forecasts.adoc
msgid ""
"This method predicts **normal household consumption**. Controlled loads such "
"as wallboxes are not included because OpenEMS plans them itself."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-daily-profiles-consumption
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/schedule/forecasts.adoc
msgid "**How it learns** (once a day, from the last 90 days):"
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-daily-profiles-consumption
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/schedule/forecasts.adoc
msgid ""
"The consumption curves of the individual days are compared and divided into "
"groups of similar days, e.g. “working day”, “weekend at home”, “away”. This "
"results in between 2 and 8 typical daily profiles."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-daily-profiles-consumption
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/schedule/forecasts.adoc
msgid ""
"It then learns **when which profile occurs**: depending on the weekday, "
"whether it is a working day, and the profile of the previous day."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-daily-profiles-consumption
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/schedule/forecasts.adoc
msgid ""
"**How it forecasts:** For today and tomorrow, the most probable profile is "
"selected. If the actual curve fits another profile significantly better in "
"the course of the day, it switches."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-daily-profiles-consumption
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/schedule/forecasts.adoc
msgid ""
"**Limits:** **Recurring** patterns are recognized. A one-off event (e.g. "
"visitors, sauna on a single day) is not predicted. At least 30 days of "
"history are necessary. After a new installation, the forecast is therefore "
"initially unavailable or inaccurate."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/schedule/forecasts.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "Weather model (solar yield)"
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-weather-model-solar-yield
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/schedule/forecasts.adoc
msgid ""
"The method learns from the past how much your **own system** produces in "
"which weather. Solar irradiation (direct and diffuse), temperature, snow and "
"time of day play a role. The orientation, shading and size of the system "
"therefore do not have to be entered; they are contained in the learned data. "
"The weather data comes from xref:user/schedule/weather.adoc[Open-Meteo]."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-weather-model-solar-yield
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/schedule/forecasts.adoc
msgid ""
"**Learning:** daily, from up to 90 days; at least 30 days are necessary."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-weather-model-solar-yield
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/schedule/forecasts.adoc
msgid "**Forecast:** 2 days, with the current weather forecast."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-weather-model-solar-yield
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/schedule/forecasts.adoc
msgid ""
"**Plausibility:** The forecast is smoothed and is never higher than the "
"power that the system has actually reached in the last 90 days. The last "
"four measured quarter hours are also included in the smoothing so that there "
"is no jump at the transition from measurement to forecast."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-weather-model-solar-yield
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/schedule/forecasts.adoc
msgid ""
"**Snow:** If the weather forecast currently reports snowfall and a snow "
"cover for at least 90 % of the forecast period, the model switches to its "
"own snow state."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-weather-model-solar-yield
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/schedule/forecasts.adoc
msgid "In the first 24 hours it continues to calculate as usual."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-weather-model-solar-yield
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/schedule/forecasts.adoc
msgid ""
"After that it uses the curve of the previous day as the forecast (“same as "
"yesterday”) if a forecast using this method is set up. Otherwise it "
"continues to calculate as usual."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-weather-model-solar-yield
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/schedule/forecasts.adoc
msgid ""
"It returns to the normal state as soon as, according to the forecast, there "
"is no more snow and none will settle. Or if, after at least 24 hours, at "
"least 30 % of a typical peak power was generated in 4 of the last 6 quarter "
"hours. The typical peak power is the value that 95 % of all quarter hours in "
"the last 90 days did not exceed."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-good-to-know
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/schedule/forecasts.adoc
msgid ""
"The learned models are not stored permanently. After a restart, OpenEMS "
"learns anew from the stored xref:user/data/history-rrd4j.adoc[history]. If "
"there is no history, there is also no basis for forecasts."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-good-to-know
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/schedule/forecasts.adoc
msgid ""
"OpenEMS records what it predicted 1, 3 or 6 hours beforehand, alongside what "
"actually happened. This makes it possible to assess the forecast quality "
"afterwards."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-good-to-know
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/schedule/forecasts.adoc
msgid ""
"Poor forecasts have a direct effect on grid-optimized charge and price "
"control."
msgstr ""
